<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Occupied Enemy Territory Administration</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1920 CE · capital Jerusalem</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British-led military government of the former Ottoman Levant after the First World War, which preceded the French and British mandates.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-allenby">Allenby</a>'s forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in December 1917 and conquered the rest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> in 1918, the occupied Ottoman territories were placed under military administration as Occupied Enemy Territory, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-law">international law</a> required until a peace settlement.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The territory was divided into zones: OETA South, roughly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, under British officers; OETA East, inland <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-transjordan">Transjordan</a>, administered by Faisal's Arab government; and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-cilicia">OETA North</a> (or West), the coast, under French officers. The administration preserved Ottoman law, restored supplies after wartime famine and began reconstruction. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ronald-storrs">Ronald Storrs</a> served as military governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1920 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-remo-conference">San Remo conference</a> assigned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations-mandate">mandates</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. OETA South was replaced by a civil administration under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herbert-samuel">Herbert Samuel</a> in July 1920, forming <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mandatory-palestine">Mandatory Palestine</a>, while France occupied inland <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> after defeating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arab-kingdom-of-syria">Arab Kingdom of Syria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/occupied-enemy-territory-administration.jpg" alt="Occupied Enemy Territory Administration" width="320" height="512"><figcaption>Image: SPQR10 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Area_of_the_OETA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jerusalem</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Edmund Allenby, Ronald Storrs</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Christianity, Judaism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>, <a href="/countries/palestine">Palestine</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a>, <a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, <a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>OETA</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=occupied-enemy-territory-administration" aria-label="Occupied Enemy Territory Administration on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5594 951 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Occupied Enemy Territory Administration lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5914 1207L5709 970M5914 1207L4997 651M5914 1207L5908 1277"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M4997 651h0M5908 1277h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5914 1207h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5914 1207h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=occupied-enemy-territory-administration">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
